Z||000000||Indy-Canada||09-16-1999||07:47 PM||||HI! I live in Nova Scotia,up here Fiero's aren't really a big thing. I have found what i think is an 84 INDY PACE CAR .It is in fair shape,it has the right interior,valve cover,wing and nose.Everything looks right but when i ran the VIN through the decoder it came backall wrong. I thought that there was only around 1550 of them made.T his came up as 176,000 of god knows how many. Is there anybody out there that knows for sure how to tell? Ineed to know ASAP because the car can be bought cheap.PLEASE HELP!! No guesses please. I don't really want it if it isn't real.Thanks for any help. INDY-CANADA||||reg||3
Z||000001||theogre||09-16-1999||08:03 PM||||VIN count is ALL Fieros made that year. the VIN sequence section is not relevant to much.<P>What did the rest of the number come out as? There are a couple people here who've seen or own pace versions now I think. They can tell you some of the other things to look for to verify it if need be.<P>For one I think they were all built with the HO(HD) 4 cyl. This motor has a number of things diferant. You may need to keep that in mind if you have to buy parts for it ever.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||09-16-1999||10:07 PM||||Check in the spair tire compartment on the drivers side wheel well. You will see a sticker with the option codes.||||reg||1
